id: portal-control
name: Portal Control
advancement: true
prerequisite: N/A
tpCost: 8
# "Instead of targeting an Opponent, you may target any Character ... and, instead of using an Attacking Maneuver, may use
# any Maneuver with an Action Cost of 1 that targets another Character as if that Character was in your Melee Range" -
# picked in its window, used through it with the distance ignored. The Grapple's move into your Melee Range is said and
# made by the table.
portalControl: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Illusion Smash may reach any Character, with any 1-Action Maneuver that targets another, as if they were in your Melee
  Range.
text: >
  Portal Control: Your ability to utilize portals grows, allowing you to do more than just attack.
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –TP Cost: 8
  –Effect: Instead of targeting an Opponent, you may target any Character with the effects of Illusion Smash and,
  instead of using an Attacking Maneuver, may use any Maneuver with an Action Cost of 1 that targets another Character
  as if that Character was in your Melee Range.

  If you would use the Grapple Maneuver through this effect and successfully enter a Grapple as a result, move the
  Grappled Character into your Melee Range on an unoccupied Square of your choice.
